The challenge for me is to make sports on TV is engaging as film or video games. If we don't, we're going to lose out. But it's the challenge I welcome. I'm gearing up for London 2012 where the games will be presented in high-definition picture and certainly in surround sound. I'll be pushing to create the best, most involving, most detailed sound ever at the Olympics, and one thing that makes me very happy is I hear that the Vuvuzillas will be banned from the games. I leave you with one of my favorite sounds, the equestering jumping event. The Sound of Sport was presented by Dennis Baxter and produced by Peregrin Andrews. It was a fallen tree production originally produced for BBC Radio 4 in 2011.
对我的挑战是让电视上的体育运动像电影或电子游戏一样引人入胜。如果我们做不到，我们就会输掉。但我欢迎这个挑战。我正在为2012年伦敦奥运会做准备，那里的比赛将以高清画质呈现，当然还有环绕声。我将努力创造奥运会上最好、最引人入胜、最详细的声音，有一件事让我非常高兴，那就是我听说呜呜祖拉（Vuvuzelas）将被禁止在运动会使用。我用我最喜欢的声音之一留给你们，马术障碍赛。体育之声由丹尼斯·巴克斯特（Dennis Baxter）呈献，佩雷格林·安德鲁斯（Peregrin Andrews）制作。它是BBC广播四台在2011年最初制作的堕落之树（Fallen Tree）作品。

